    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"310045\">@Eric Wieser</span> Thank you. I think that is an excellent suggestion.</p>\n<p>However, among the code I currently have at hand, I could not find an example where mid-loop invariants would be genuinely useful. Conceptually, though, it seems plausible that such examples exist, so I will keep looking for one.</p>",
        "id": 614194392,
        "sender_full_name": "Asei Inoue",
        "timestamp": 1785697822
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thanks for giving the syntax a read already :) It's not formally released yet, mostly because it builds on the as-of-yet unreleased <code>vcgen</code> and its <code>Std.Internal</code> metatheory and for a lack of documentation.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>it would make it clearer at which point the condition is expected to hold</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I don't think I agree with this. Note that the invariant is not a mere <code>assert</code>; it also holds <em>on loop exit</em>! Thus, it is actually a bit more confusing to put it inside the <code>do</code> block. Besides, the same place will also need to accomodate the <code>decreasing</code> variant for <code>while</code> loops, and that would be weird to place in the body as well.</p>\n<p>For comparison (thanks, Claude), Velvet, Dafny, Boogie, Verus, Viper, Eiffel, JML put it before the loop body. Why3, SPARK, Prusti, Nagini put it in the body.</p>",
        "id": 614485979,
        "sender_full_name": "Sebastian Graf",
        "timestamp": 1785832020
    },
